1
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:03,960
Why are you helping me?

2
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:06,520
I need a capable man like you on my side.

3
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:09,320
For your first job, get rid of Thatri.

4
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,040
<i>I'm nearly healed.</i>

5
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,520
<i>I won't be bothering you much longer.</i>

6
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:21,240
<i>See you in Phuket, Leopard.</i>

7
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:23,240
I guess it's almost time for me to go.

8
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,320
How dare you speak
to your mother like this?

9
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,080
Who taught you to be so rebellious?!

10
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:29,040
I'm sorry.

11
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:31,240
But if anyone taught me this,

12
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:33,680
it's my own life experiences

13
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,560
that taught me.

14
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,600
Is something wrong?

15
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:48,680
Was I a bit too harsh during dinner?

16
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,640
Not at all. I'm just surprised.

17
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:56,080
I never thought you would choose me.

18
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:59,880
Thinking about it,

19
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,960
Tri was right.

20
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,080
My life belongs to me,

21
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,840
and I must choose for myself.

22
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:10,520
And I chose my husband.

23
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:15,520
I'm so happy.

24
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:18,720
Do you realize
you just called me your husband?

25
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,440
Is that wrong? Since we are…

26
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:25,120
Not at all.

27
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,840
But you know what?

28
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,240
You just made me love you even more.

29
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:33,800
So you didn't love me before?

30
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:38,240
I did. But now…

31
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,400
I love you so, so much.

32
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:29,760
Here's an extra reward.

33
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,040
Thank you.

34
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,680
Ever since the war ended,

35
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:40,480
it seems your profits
have been soaring, Mr. Vijarn.

36
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,960
"Mr. Vijarn"?

37
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,200
You adapt quickly.

38
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,840
Of course, my profits are good.

39
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:51,880
Ms. Fuangfah is gone,

40
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:55,440
and without those Japanese soldiers,
everything is much easier to manage.

41
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,120
That leaves only Thatri
and the district chief.

42
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,920
And the first one we must eliminate

43
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,520
is Thatri.

44
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,800
Should I go and kill him right now?

45
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:06,960
Hold your horses.

46
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,440
We failed last time.

47
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:12,600
This time, we must plan carefully,
and make sure we don't screw up again.

48
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,720
Dad!

49
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,800
You're here early.

50
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:40,000
Is something the matter?

51
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,080
Yes.

52
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:46,400
I've got all the property
transfer documents ready for you.

53
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:49,760
Thank you.

54
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,400
Now that everything is settled,

55
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:58,120
will you be returning
to Bangkok right away?

56
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:09,480
I've noticed you've faced
so many hardships

57
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:11,640
since coming to Phuket.

58
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:14,000
You'd have a much easier life
back in Bangkok.

59
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,440
I suppose so.

60
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,880
Mr. Thatri.

61
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,400
Before you leave,

62
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,960
since you are Miss Rajit's elder relative…

63
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:45,680
may I

64
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:49,200
officially pursue her?

65
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,720
You may.

66
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:22,400
-If you'll excuse me.
-Of course.

67
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:08,800
Pretty soon, it'll be
just the two of us left,

68
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,120
Don Jose.

69
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,480
What's wrong?

70
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:30,120
Why didn't you go inside
to get the transfer documents?

71
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:40,080
I'm going to be left all alone
in this house soon anyway.

72
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,720
There's no need to rush.

73
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,920
Well, you have Mr. Vijarn.

74
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,840
He's liked you for a long time.

75
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:53,960
You two are a perfect match.

76
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,720
But I don't love him.

77
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:06,720
I'd rather live here alone.

78
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:13,880
Can't you just stay here
and not go back to Bangkok?

79
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:22,640
I want to stay with you
for a long time too.

80
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:29,240
Can't it be forever?

81
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:39,160
No.

82
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:41,200
It's impossible.

83
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,680
What were you even hoping for, Rajit?

84
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:00,880
It's just impossible.

85
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:24,960
<i>I'm nearly healed.</i>
<i>I won't be bothering you much longer.</i>

86
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:27,680
<i>See you in Phuket, Leopard.</i>

87
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:11,240
Please eat something, Mother.

88
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:14,760
You haven't eaten anything
since this morning.

89
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,640
Mother,

90
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,560
please talk to me.

91
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:26,880
I'll leave you alone then.

92
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,760
You defied me so blatantly,

93
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:32,680
and now you act sweet? I'm not giving in.

94
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:38,760
Oh, Mother,

95
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:41,720
please understand. I'm married now.

96
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:44,160
I must stay with my husband.

97
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:46,880
How can you expect me to abandon him?

98
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:49,840
Oh, stop talking. You're frustrating me.

99
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:08,440
When is the food I ordered coming?
I'm starving.

100
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:11,480
We ran out of ingredients, ma'am.
The supply boat just arrived,

101
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:14,480
and we sent someone to get them.
Please wait just a moment.

102
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,360
Such a backward town.

103
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,240
If she wasn't so obsessed
with her husband…

104
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:32,800
Tri.

105
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,840
Are you looking for something to eat?

106
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:38,680
I'm at a restaurant.

107
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:40,640
I certainly didn't come here
to sit around.

108
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,040
I see.

109
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:45,320
Did you say something to Sasi?

110
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,280
She became so aggressive with me.

111
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,920
Does expressing one's own opinion

112
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,800
mean being aggressive?

113
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,360
Then when you order her around

114
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:58,920
and force her to do this and that,

115
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,400
what should we call it?

116
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,920
Are you saying that I'm controlling her?

117
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,760
Well, if I'm being honest, yes, I am.

118
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:08,200
Tri!

119
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,280
You must be resentful because I forced her

120
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:16,280
to break off the engagement.

121
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:19,040
But you can't blame me.

122
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:21,760
It's your own fault
for foolishly going bankrupt.

123
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:25,200
My daughter would be miserable with you.

124
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,920
I don't hold a grudge or blame you.

125
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,640
Nor will I badmouth you
to the district chief.

126
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:33,960
Reflecting on it,

127
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:37,160
I actually think I'm lucky
that I don't have to tolerate you.

128
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,520
Tri!

129
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,520
-You!
-Your food is here.

130
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,080
I'm not eating anymore.

131
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,640
I'll take it then.

132
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:58,000
Yes, sir.

133
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:17,280
Poor yet so full of pride. Idiot.

134
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,640
-Bring me the bill.
-Yes, ma'am.

135
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,360
Let me take care of that, ma'am.

136
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,160
Who are you?

137
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,520
Why are you suddenly treating me?

138
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,240
I'm the lawyer for Mr. Thatri's family.

139
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:36,440
Lawyer?

140
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:40,320
He's broke. How can he even afford one?

141
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:42,800
Broke?

142
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:46,520
I couldn't tell
that Mr. Thatri had no money.

143
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:49,480
That's just his old facade.

144
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:52,440
He used to be filthy rich,
wealthy beyond belief.

145
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:55,000
Everyone in Bangkok knows Thatri.

146
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:58,000
Too bad his stupid decisions
left him completely broke.

147
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:26,320
You called for me, sir?

148
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,560
I'm heading to Bangkok.

149
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:31,920
I'm leaving you in charge.

150
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:35,680
Take good care of everything,
and ensure no mistakes are made.

151
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:38,920
Yes, sir.

152
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:42,360
Why the sudden trip to Bangkok?

153
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:44,640
I'm going to dig into Thatri's past.

154
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:48,080
It seems luck is on our side.

155
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:52,760
Maybe I can get rid of him
without wasting a single bullet.

156
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:11,240
Peel those prawns carefully.

157
00:17:11,319 --> 00:17:12,800
Got it.

158
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:14,560
Primprao.

159
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:16,640
Do you know how to do it?

160
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:18,960
Of course, I do.

161
00:17:20,599 --> 00:17:22,839
I'm going to make
stir-fried stink beans with prawns.

162
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,839
I guarantee it'll be delicious.

163
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:27,839
I've missed your cooking so much.

164
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:31,120
It'll taste great
because I peeled the onions.

165
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,040
Well, then my part
will be just as delicious,

166
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,520
because I'm the one
slicing the stink beans.

167
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:40,240
Right.

168
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:42,440
Neither of you ever wants to lose…

169
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:50,240
I'm heading to Bangkok soon.

170
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:53,720
And why are you telling me this?

171
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:58,160
You'd accuse me
of leaving you behind without a word.

172
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:01,080
Since you're leaving anyway,

173
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:03,440
why don't you just leave today?

174
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:08,840
Hey. Uncle Ree is your elder.

175
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,600
How can you talk back to him like that?

176
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,720
Have a safe trip, Uncle Ree.

177
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,240
Rajit,

178
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,520
hurry up and say goodbye to him.

179
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:37,320
I'll be off then.
See you when I return to Phuket.

180
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,520
Yes, Uncle Ree.

181
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:51,880
Why were you being so passive-aggressive?

182
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,560
I wasn't.

183
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:58,800
Uncle Ree keeps pushing me
toward Mr. Vijarn,

184
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:01,200
but I don't even like him.

185
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:06,040
Do you dislike Mr. Vijarn,
or are you in love with Uncle Ree?

186
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,640
It's nothing like that.

187
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:13,960
Right, of course. Uncle Ree is your uncle.

188
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:16,080
How could you have feelings
for your own uncle?

189
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:19,040
Exactly. Because Uncle Ree belongs to me.

190
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:21,400
-He's mine.
-He's mine.

191
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:22,320
He's mine.

192
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:24,480
-He's mine.
-Since when?

193
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:27,080
Since the very first day I met Uncle Ree.

194
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,840
I told you, I claimed him first.

195
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:30,000
I claimed him too.

196
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,440
I claimed him first.

197
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:33,520
No way.

198
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:38,840
And there she goes.

199
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,440
What is wrong with her today?

200
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:45,360
PHRA NAKHON

201
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:07,080
Leopard!

202
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:13,720
Wild Bull.

203
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:15,840
You look much better, just as you said.

204
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:19,720
Of course. I had to recover
as fast as possible.

205
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:22,440
I've left my burdens
with you for too long.

206
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:26,760
Here you go. Burden transferred.

207
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:29,160
The documents are completely finalized.

208
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:33,120
Really?

209
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:35,760
Thank you so much, man.

210
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:36,880
Yeah.

211
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,440
Are we returning to Phuket today?

212
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:41,840
You want me to go back with you?

213
00:20:44,320 --> 00:20:45,160
That would be best.

214
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:47,440
I don't want to get caught
and end up in prison.

215
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,640
You have a point.

216
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:54,760
Let me pack my bags real quick.

217
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:56,480
-Sure.
-Come in. Let's head inside.

218
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,600
Let's go, my friend.

219
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:05,640
Be careful.

220
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:07,040
Sure.

221
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:12,200
Mom!

222
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,040
Mom!

223
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:19,680
Mom!

224
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:22,000
Mom. Mom.

225
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:23,720
We need to get her to the hospital.

226
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,600
Let me help you.

227
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:28,360
Mom.

228
00:21:33,760 --> 00:21:37,440
Following the appendectomy,
she will need to recover for several days.

229
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:41,240
Thank you, Doctor.

230
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:42,400
You're welcome.

231
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:53,680
I'll have to head back
to Phuket by myself.

232
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,400
You stay here and look after her.

233
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:58,840
Wait until she fully recovers
before you follow me.

234
00:22:04,080 --> 00:22:05,760
Am I causing you trouble again?

235
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:08,960
Don't worry about it.

236
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:24,720
THE NATIONAL LIBRARY

237
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:32,480
Sorry. Could I look through the archived
newspapers from the past two years?

238
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:34,760
Oh, certainly. Right this way.

239
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:41,400
This way.

240
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:53,720
Here you go.
The issues from the past two years.

241
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:55,440
-Thank you very much.
-You're welcome.

242
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:26,680
MR. THATRI THATRIPAN

243
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:31,680
MR. THATRI THATRIPAN, THE BILLIONAIRE

244
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:34,560
DONATES 1,000 BAHT

245
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:36,360
TO FLOOD VICTIMS IN THE NORTH

246
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:44,000
Finally.

247
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:46,120
THE BILLIONAIRE

248
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:07,000
I promise I'll get there shortly.

249
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,320
Just hurry up.

250
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:11,720
If I get caught, it's on you.

251
00:24:12,360 --> 00:24:14,160
Yeah, don't worry.

252
00:24:14,240 --> 00:24:16,000
I'm coming soon.

253
00:24:18,360 --> 00:24:19,320
I'm off, Wild Bull.

254
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:21,680
-Take care, my friend. Safe travels.
-Yeah.

255
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:53,000
Wild Bull.

256
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:58,280
What would you say
if I told you I like your niece?

257
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:07,240
What did you just say?
I couldn't hear you.

258
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:08,560
I said…

259
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:13,760
It's nothing.

260
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,520
Alright, have a safe trip.

261
00:25:18,120 --> 00:25:21,200
Keep an eye out for some pretty ladies
for me while you're there.

262
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:23,320
What for?

263
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,480
Well,

264
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,040
once I'm rich,

265
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:30,040
girls will be chasing after me
just like they did to you.

266
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:32,840
Me back then?

267
00:25:33,480 --> 00:25:34,680
What's so great about it?

268
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:38,120
Now that I'm broke,
nobody even glances at me.

269
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:41,560
But I've never even had a girlfriend.

270
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:44,000
Being poor

271
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,200
made me too insecure to care for anyone.

272
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:50,840
But who knew? Suddenly,
I became rich out of nowhere,

273
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:53,480
even when I thought
I'd never get the chance.

274
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:56,800
So, you're giving me a pep talk now?

275
00:25:57,760 --> 00:25:59,080
Damn right.

276
00:26:00,280 --> 00:26:01,480
Going from rich to bankrupt

277
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:04,920
doesn't mean you can't
get rich again, Leopard.

278
00:26:17,240 --> 00:26:19,320
Once this mess is over,
I'll head to Chiang Mai

279
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:21,320
to rebuild my fortune. And…

280
00:26:23,800 --> 00:26:25,440
If it's not too late…

281
00:26:26,080 --> 00:26:27,080
Too late for what?

282
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:30,200
It's nothing.

283
00:26:30,280 --> 00:26:32,960
I must go, or I'll miss my train.
Catch you later, Wild Bull.

284
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:34,160
See you, my friend.

285
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:58,840
PHUKET

286
00:27:08,480 --> 00:27:09,480
Rajit.

287
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,760
THE BILLIONAIRE DONATES 1,000 BAHT
TO FLOOD VICTIMS IN THE NORTH

288
00:27:22,760 --> 00:27:24,160
What is the meaning of this?

289
00:27:26,080 --> 00:27:28,800
MR. THATRI THATRIPAN, THE BILLIONAIRE

290
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:30,880
DONATES 1,000 BAHT

291
00:27:30,960 --> 00:27:33,080
TO FLOOD VICTIMS IN THE NORTH

292
00:27:41,560 --> 00:27:43,160
Don't go over the budget.

293
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:44,480
-Yes, ma'am.
-Times are tough.

294
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:46,320
Okay? Oh, Vijarn?

295
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:48,800
What happened?
What are the police doing here?

296
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:50,160
You probably don't know yet,

297
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:52,920
but an impostor is living among us.

298
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,840
I brought the police to arrest him
before he causes any more trouble.

299
00:27:55,920 --> 00:27:58,600
Hold on. What impostor
are you talking about?

300
00:27:58,680 --> 00:28:02,160
I'm here every day,
and I haven't seen a single stranger.

301
00:28:02,240 --> 00:28:04,480
It's Thatri. He's an impostor.

302
00:28:04,560 --> 00:28:06,840
He's not Mr. Som's real nephew.

303
00:28:07,960 --> 00:28:10,720
No way. I've served Thatri
for almost a year.

304
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:13,360
He's a good man. He can't be an impostor.

305
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:15,400
I've handed all the evidence
over to Miss Rajit.

306
00:28:15,480 --> 00:28:17,640
As for the details,
I'll explain them later.

307
00:28:17,720 --> 00:28:20,320
Right now, I'm going to drag him to jail.

308
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:21,560
This way, officers.

309
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:24,120
Hey.

310
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:28,040
-Let's go after them.
-Right, right.

311
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:28,960
What is he talking about?

312
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:31,040
THE BILLIONAIRE DONATES 1,000 BAHT

313
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:34,000
TO FLOOD VICTIMS IN THE NORTH

314
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,640
Answer me.

315
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:39,520
Are you the same person in this picture?

316
00:28:42,920 --> 00:28:44,560
Why won't you speak?

317
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:51,880
Yes, that's me.

318
00:28:57,360 --> 00:28:59,840
"Mr. Thatri Thatripan.

319
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:03,440
The Billionaire

320
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:05,480
donates 1,000 baht

321
00:29:05,560 --> 00:29:07,960
to flood victims in the north."

322
00:29:09,440 --> 00:29:11,760
A thousand baht is no small amount.

323
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:14,320
For a high school graduate

324
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:16,360
working as a government clerk,

325
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:19,080
that's nearly an entire year's salary.

326
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:23,200
Am I right, Mr. Thatri?

327
00:29:27,760 --> 00:29:29,040
I never wanted to lie to you.

328
00:29:29,120 --> 00:29:30,800
Then what is it that you want?

329
00:29:32,120 --> 00:29:34,480
I'm friends with the real Thatri.

330
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:36,640
He was injured and couldn't come
to claim his inheritance,

331
00:29:37,160 --> 00:29:38,480
so he sent me in his place.

332
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:42,000
Is that your explanation?

333
00:29:42,080 --> 00:29:45,240
Isn't that too convenient?
You went bankrupt

334
00:29:46,440 --> 00:29:48,400
and used an identical name

335
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:50,840
to fraud your way into this inheritance.

336
00:29:51,920 --> 00:29:53,680
I read all about you,

337
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:55,880
but I wanted to hear it from you,

338
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:57,720
hoping you'd admit your guilt

339
00:29:57,800 --> 00:30:00,400
instead of making up excuses like this.

340
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:02,320
I'm not making excuses.

341
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:08,320
Rajit. Rajit.

342
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:11,800
Rajit. Rajit.

343
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,240
-Rajit.
-Officers, arrest him.

344
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:19,720
This is him.
He's pretending to be Mr. Thatri

345
00:30:19,800 --> 00:30:22,320
for the inheritance.
He's just trying to steal it.

346
00:30:22,400 --> 00:30:23,800
Take him to the police station.

347
00:30:26,440 --> 00:30:27,640
Thatri.

348
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:31,240
Are you really an impostor,
just as Vijarn claims?

349
00:30:36,280 --> 00:30:37,160
Yes, I am.

350
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:39,440
Heard that loud and clear?

351
00:30:40,360 --> 00:30:42,920
He's a fraud who stole the money.

352
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:45,400
-What did I steal?
-The monthly salary you received

353
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:48,080
and the central funds
you took to buy tin ore.

354
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:51,640
It totals over a hundred thousand baht.
If that isn't stealing, what is?

355
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:54,040
I may be an impostor,
but I never stole anything.

356
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:56,960
Then prove it.

357
00:30:57,640 --> 00:31:00,560
I have a witness. Go ask the District…

358
00:31:03,960 --> 00:31:06,040
District who? Say it.

359
00:31:06,120 --> 00:31:07,520
Speak up.

360
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:11,360
Give us all the names.
Because if this is a case of collusion,

361
00:31:11,440 --> 00:31:13,200
you can all rot in jail together.

362
00:31:15,400 --> 00:31:16,720
Mr. Thatri

363
00:31:18,320 --> 00:31:19,560
Thatripan.

364
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,360
You know who I am?

365
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:23,480
You may not know me,

366
00:31:23,560 --> 00:31:25,840
but a prominent socialite like you?

367
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:27,960
I know you all too well.

368
00:31:29,160 --> 00:31:30,400
Why are you silent?

369
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,440
Since everything is crystal clear now,

370
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:39,320
let me take him to the station.

371
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:40,440
Hold on.

372
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:44,960
Miss Rajit, you cannot help him with this.

373
00:31:45,040 --> 00:31:46,840
This is a criminal offense.

374
00:32:02,200 --> 00:32:04,000
Take me away, officers.

375
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:11,880
Thank you.

376
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:14,920
Knowing you still care is enough for me.

377
00:32:21,120 --> 00:32:23,320
Officers, take him away.

378
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,720
What is going on, ,iss?

379
00:32:57,800 --> 00:32:59,920
How can Thatri be an impostor?

380
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:02,600
This has to be a mistake, right, miss?

381
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:17,600
Tri got arrested?

382
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:18,720
Yes.

383
00:33:18,800 --> 00:33:21,320
His secret was exposed,
so they arrested him.

384
00:33:22,680 --> 00:33:24,040
What secret was exposed, Sasi?

385
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:27,560
Uh…

386
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:32,440
Tri posed as his friend
to claim an inheritance in Phuket.

387
00:33:32,520 --> 00:33:34,440
But he didn't swindle anyone, Mother.

388
00:33:34,520 --> 00:33:36,320
His friend knew all about it.

389
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:40,280
He's still a fool. Foolish as always.

390
00:33:40,360 --> 00:33:42,680
Always looking for trouble for himself.

391
00:33:42,760 --> 00:33:44,600
He hasn't changed.

392
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:48,480
Still, Tri is my friend.

393
00:33:49,520 --> 00:33:51,880
I'm going to visit him, Mother.

394
00:33:51,960 --> 00:33:54,400
If you see him,
pass this message to Tri for me.

395
00:33:54,480 --> 00:33:56,680
Being broke is bad enough,

396
00:33:57,560 --> 00:34:00,080
but being broke
and living a lie is just pitiful.

397
00:34:00,600 --> 00:34:02,280
Impersonating someone for money

398
00:34:02,360 --> 00:34:05,080
and then having the nerve
to waste more on a lawyer?

399
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:06,680
What a reckless squanderer.

400
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:13,560
Let's hurry up and go.

401
00:34:15,440 --> 00:34:16,639
Right.

402
00:34:25,239 --> 00:34:26,679
THALANG PROVINCIAL POLICE STATION

403
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:29,080
No wonder. I was just wondering

404
00:34:29,159 --> 00:34:30,920
who told Mr. Vijarn about this.

405
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:34,800
I'm so sorry on behalf of my mother, Tri.

406
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:38,400
It's alright. She didn't do it on purpose.

407
00:34:38,480 --> 00:34:40,760
Mr. Vijarn likely tricked her
into telling him.

408
00:34:41,920 --> 00:34:44,120
Why would he trick her?

409
00:34:45,880 --> 00:34:47,480
Is he intentionally targeting you?

410
00:34:50,600 --> 00:34:53,480
Let's not dwell on his motives right now.

411
00:34:53,560 --> 00:34:56,159
You should focus
on getting Tri out of here first.

412
00:34:58,880 --> 00:35:01,440
I'll testify for you.
I'll state that I knew everything,

413
00:35:01,520 --> 00:35:03,640
and you had no bad intentions.

414
00:35:04,240 --> 00:35:06,480
-You'd better not do that.
-Why?

415
00:35:07,560 --> 00:35:10,440
If I'm right, this was a setup
from the very start.

416
00:35:10,520 --> 00:35:13,200
His target is me,
but if the district chief steps forward,

417
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:14,680
you might get dragged down too.

418
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:18,800
But you've done so much. I managed
to defeat the pirates because of you.

419
00:35:18,880 --> 00:35:21,360
How can I just leave you
behind bars like this?

420
00:35:22,920 --> 00:35:25,080
Official duty and identity fraud

421
00:35:25,160 --> 00:35:26,400
are two different things.

422
00:35:29,040 --> 00:35:31,000
And I have a favor to ask you.

423
00:35:32,240 --> 00:35:33,360
Just say the word.

424
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,880
I doubt anyone will bail Mr. Thatri out.

425
00:35:43,960 --> 00:35:46,880
We're just waiting
for the time to place him in remand.

426
00:35:49,760 --> 00:35:51,400
But don't worry, Miss Rajit.

427
00:35:51,480 --> 00:35:54,560
I won't let him
cause any more trouble here.

428
00:35:55,640 --> 00:35:58,000
By the way, do you happen to know

429
00:35:58,080 --> 00:36:00,640
where the real Thatri is?

430
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:03,880
I have no idea.

431
00:36:04,480 --> 00:36:06,680
But either way, it doesn't matter anymore.

432
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:09,640
The deadline for the real Mr. Thatri

433
00:36:09,720 --> 00:36:11,720
to claim the inheritance has passed.

434
00:36:13,480 --> 00:36:16,960
Wherever he is, or if he even exists,

435
00:36:17,040 --> 00:36:18,800
it changes nothing.

436
00:36:19,800 --> 00:36:23,160
The entire fortune belongs only to you.

437
00:36:28,760 --> 00:36:30,880
With such a massive fortune,

438
00:36:32,480 --> 00:36:34,480
I can't possibly manage it all on my own.

439
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:54,040
Don't be afraid, Miss Rajit.

440
00:36:54,120 --> 00:36:55,600
I will be by your side to help you.

441
00:36:56,800 --> 00:36:57,840
Not just with work,

442
00:36:59,640 --> 00:37:02,520
but I will never let anyone
hurt you ever again.

443
00:37:53,960 --> 00:37:55,120
This way, please.

444
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:02,520
Mr. Thatri, you have a visitor.

445
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:05,240
-Go ahead.
-Thank you.

446
00:38:09,760 --> 00:38:11,040
Who are you?

447
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:13,360
I'm the new employee.

448
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:16,120
Miss Rajit asked me
to bring some food to you.

449
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:19,400
Why did she send you?
What about the others?

450
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:23,960
She didn't want to draw any attention.

451
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:30,680
Here, she sent this for you.

452
00:38:35,600 --> 00:38:36,560
Thanks.

453
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:38,400
You're welcome.

454
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:59,200
I have complete control
over Som Song Saeng House now.

455
00:38:59,800 --> 00:39:03,080
As for Thatri, he wouldn't dare ask
the District Chief or anyone for help.

456
00:39:03,160 --> 00:39:04,440
Because if he does,

457
00:39:04,520 --> 00:39:08,440
I'll drag whoever helps him behind bars
right along with him.

458
00:39:08,520 --> 00:39:09,840
Very meticulous.

459
00:39:09,920 --> 00:39:13,480
By using the law instead of violence,

460
00:39:13,560 --> 00:39:15,600
he won't be able to touch you at all.

461
00:39:16,160 --> 00:39:18,160
And who said I would only use the law?

462
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:24,640
Now that he is behind bars,

463
00:39:25,760 --> 00:39:27,560
he's like a fish in a barrel.

464
00:39:29,240 --> 00:39:31,840
Why leave him alive to bother us?

465
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:45,720
Excuse me, sir.

466
00:39:46,800 --> 00:39:49,640
An inmate is having a seizure
and foaming at the mouth.

467
00:40:01,960 --> 00:40:03,040
Mr. Thatri.

468
00:40:05,760 --> 00:40:06,920
Are you alright?

469
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:09,360
It was a close call, District Chief.

470
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:11,240
But…

471
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:13,600
you seem completely fine.

472
00:40:13,680 --> 00:40:16,920
The police informed me
that you were poisoned.

473
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:19,000
There was an attempt.

474
00:40:20,560 --> 00:40:21,920
But Mr. Thatri was not affected.

475
00:40:23,160 --> 00:40:24,600
What exactly happened?

476
00:40:35,680 --> 00:40:36,720
Hey.

477
00:40:37,480 --> 00:40:39,600
-Give it back.
-Hell no.

478
00:40:39,680 --> 00:40:42,440
It looks delicious.
How can you keep it all to yourself?

479
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:44,560
If you want some, just ask nicely.

480
00:40:44,640 --> 00:40:47,160
This is how we ask.
Got a problem with that?

481
00:40:47,240 --> 00:40:48,880
Don't be so stingy with food.

482
00:40:48,960 --> 00:40:52,400
No way you're enjoying this alone.

483
00:40:52,480 --> 00:40:54,040
Let's eat. I'm starving.

484
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:00,320
It's good, huh?

485
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:05,680
Are you two starving or what?

486
00:41:44,360 --> 00:41:47,840
Help! Someone has been poisoned!

487
00:41:49,240 --> 00:41:51,040
Could it be Zhang Gong Cheng?

488
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:54,080
He might have found out
you were arrested and wanted revenge.

489
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:55,760
That's possible.

490
00:41:55,840 --> 00:41:58,680
But one thing is for sure.
He didn't act alone.

491
00:41:59,360 --> 00:42:00,440
How can you be so sure?

492
00:42:03,160 --> 00:42:04,960
The person who brought the poisoned food

493
00:42:05,560 --> 00:42:08,160
used Rajit's name
so I would lower my guard.

494
00:42:08,840 --> 00:42:10,840
This means they must know the ins and outs

495
00:42:10,920 --> 00:42:12,960
of Som Song Saeng House quite well.

496
00:42:13,040 --> 00:42:15,600
Zhang Gong Cheng
couldn't possibly know that much.

497
00:42:17,040 --> 00:42:18,800
Someone from Som Song Saeng House?

498
00:42:20,280 --> 00:42:21,560
Who do you suspect?

499
00:42:25,520 --> 00:42:27,440
I need a bit more evidence.

500
00:42:29,360 --> 00:42:31,120
I still don't understand

501
00:42:31,720 --> 00:42:33,080
why he did all of this.

502
00:42:45,120 --> 00:42:48,320
How on earth did he survive that?
That bastard is too lucky.

503
00:42:49,760 --> 00:42:51,200
I will strike again tonight.

504
00:42:51,280 --> 00:42:53,600
-This time, I won't fail.
-Too risky.

505
00:42:54,160 --> 00:42:56,120
The police will definitely
protect him closely.

506
00:42:57,440 --> 00:42:59,280
Let's wait for a better moment.

507
00:43:06,240 --> 00:43:07,680
The roses you ordered are here.

508
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:14,040
Even though the war is over,

509
00:43:14,120 --> 00:43:15,680
a bouquet this big

510
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:18,320
must have cost a fortune.

511
00:43:18,400 --> 00:43:20,000
I'm giving these to Rajit.

512
00:43:22,160 --> 00:43:24,120
Do you actually like her that much?

513
00:43:27,560 --> 00:43:31,000
I never liked her.
The only reason I'm pursuing her

514
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:34,400
is to prevent anyone there
from noticing or suspecting my operations.

515
00:43:36,520 --> 00:43:38,080
And more importantly…

516
00:43:46,400 --> 00:43:47,960
<i>Mr. Som…</i>

517
00:43:48,600 --> 00:43:50,400
Please don't seize my boat.

518
00:43:50,480 --> 00:43:53,760
If you take it away,
how am I supposed to earn a living?

519
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:55,720
If you don't want it seized,

520
00:43:55,800 --> 00:43:57,600
then pay back your debt.

521
00:43:57,680 --> 00:43:59,120
Well…

522
00:44:00,240 --> 00:44:02,920
I don't have the money right now.
Could I postpone the payment?

523
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:06,040
No way. I have countless debtors.

524
00:44:06,640 --> 00:44:09,920
If I let everyone postpone,
I'd go bankrupt.

525
00:44:11,960 --> 00:44:14,120
Mr. Som, I beg of you. Please.

526
00:44:14,200 --> 00:44:15,280
-Dad.
-Mr. Som.

527
00:44:15,360 --> 00:44:17,160
Don't seize my boat.

528
00:44:17,240 --> 00:44:19,040
This boat is my entire life.

529
00:44:19,120 --> 00:44:22,280
I'm seizing your boat regardless.

530
00:44:24,240 --> 00:44:25,760
-Mr. Som. Please.
-Dad.

531
00:44:25,840 --> 00:44:26,640
-Don't take it.
-Dad.

532
00:44:26,720 --> 00:44:27,720
-Please…
-Argh!

533
00:44:29,840 --> 00:44:31,840
Dad, you don't need to go this far.

534
00:44:31,920 --> 00:44:33,880
-It's alright, son. It's fine.
-Dad.

535
00:44:33,960 --> 00:44:35,880
Mr. Som, please don't take my boat.

536
00:44:35,960 --> 00:44:37,160
-Mr. Som.
-Get off!

537
00:44:37,240 --> 00:44:38,440
-Don't seize it.
-Get off!

538
00:44:38,520 --> 00:44:39,960
-Please, don't seize my boat.
-Hey.

539
00:44:40,040 --> 00:44:41,680
-Hey.
-Let go of him.

540
00:45:12,240 --> 00:45:15,920
Dad… I brought you some noodles.

541
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:24,360
Dad! Dad!

542
00:45:25,360 --> 00:45:26,240
Dad.

543
00:45:27,080 --> 00:45:28,480
Dad.

544
00:45:28,560 --> 00:45:31,040
Why did you have to do this?

545
00:45:31,120 --> 00:45:33,440
Dad. Get up.

546
00:45:33,520 --> 00:45:36,000
Dad, please get up.

547
00:45:39,000 --> 00:45:41,040
Dad!

548
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:43,080
Dad…

549
00:45:47,960 --> 00:45:50,560
Dad!

550
00:46:04,760 --> 00:46:07,480
Alright, Rajit. Hold on tight to Grandpa.

551
00:46:07,560 --> 00:46:08,760
-I'm going to make you fly.
-Okay.

552
00:46:08,840 --> 00:46:12,280
Ready? One, two, three, fly!

553
00:46:12,360 --> 00:46:13,440
Yay!

554
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:39,120
I practically bled dry just to graduate.

555
00:46:39,200 --> 00:46:41,560
I endured his constant abuse
and worked under him

556
00:46:41,640 --> 00:46:43,320
just to stay close.

557
00:46:43,400 --> 00:46:46,320
Then, I used all his connections
to make myself rich,

558
00:46:47,560 --> 00:46:49,360
while he never knew who I actually was.

559
00:46:52,000 --> 00:46:54,120
I truly admire your patience.

560
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:58,680
Thanks, but I want more than that.

561
00:46:59,720 --> 00:47:01,520
My goal

562
00:47:01,600 --> 00:47:03,520
is to wipe out their entire bloodline.

563
00:47:03,600 --> 00:47:05,600
Since he was so greedy for money,

564
00:47:05,680 --> 00:47:07,960
I'll take everything and make it mine.

565
00:47:08,040 --> 00:47:09,880
I will ruin the granddaughter
he loved so dearly,

566
00:47:09,960 --> 00:47:13,520
destroying her completely,
before tossing her aside like an old rag.

567
00:47:16,280 --> 00:47:19,680
But what a damn shame,
the old bastard died early

568
00:47:20,520 --> 00:47:22,480
and didn't live to see it
with his own eyes.

569
00:47:44,840 --> 00:47:46,520
Uncle Ree! Please help me!

570
00:48:05,400 --> 00:48:07,200
-Hey! What's that?
-Let's go, Rajit.

571
00:48:07,280 --> 00:48:08,600
Jump!

572
00:48:20,760 --> 00:48:22,120
You went bankrupt

573
00:48:23,320 --> 00:48:25,280
and used an identical name

574
00:48:25,360 --> 00:48:27,880
to fraud your way into this inheritance.

575
00:48:28,960 --> 00:48:30,560
I read all about you,

576
00:48:30,640 --> 00:48:32,760
but I wanted to hear it from you,

577
00:48:33,360 --> 00:48:34,600
hoping you'd admit your guilt

578
00:48:34,680 --> 00:48:37,080
instead of making up excuses like this.

579
00:48:39,760 --> 00:48:42,920
Just catching a glimpse of him
made me want to cry.

580
00:48:43,000 --> 00:48:46,160
-I feel so sorry for Mr. Thatri, Grandma.
-If you break the law,

581
00:48:46,240 --> 00:48:48,960
-that's what you get. Keep that in mind.
-Ouch.

582
00:48:49,040 --> 00:48:51,240
But he was always so good to us, Grandma.

583
00:48:51,840 --> 00:48:54,320
That's exactly why I went to visit him.

584
00:48:54,400 --> 00:48:58,560
Kindness is one thing, but it doesn't give
anyone the right to break the law.

585
00:48:59,400 --> 00:49:01,600
Let's go. Oh.

586
00:49:05,360 --> 00:49:06,560
Miss Rajit.

587
00:49:08,680 --> 00:49:10,360
Who are those flowers from?

588
00:49:12,280 --> 00:49:14,120
Mr. Vijarn gave them to me.

589
00:49:17,440 --> 00:49:19,920
Miss Rajit, I just went to visit Thatri.

590
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:21,600
-I feel sorry for him.
-Nid.

591
00:49:24,760 --> 00:49:27,280
I don't want to hear anything
about a fraud

592
00:49:27,360 --> 00:49:29,760
who is only after someone else's fortune.

593
00:49:34,920 --> 00:49:36,680
And what about these flowers?

594
00:49:39,520 --> 00:49:41,440
Do whatever you want with them.

595
00:49:54,600 --> 00:49:56,120
She's probably just angry.

596
00:49:56,200 --> 00:49:58,320
After all, she was deceived
for nearly a year.

597
00:50:01,120 --> 00:50:02,600
Don't hold it against her.

598
00:50:03,480 --> 00:50:06,400
I'm not upset with her.
I actually feel sorry for her.

599
00:50:06,480 --> 00:50:08,600
She was closest to Mr. Thatri.

600
00:50:08,680 --> 00:50:10,600
She must be devastated.

601
00:50:12,720 --> 00:50:15,000
Anyway, how is that bastard doing?

602
00:50:16,160 --> 00:50:18,080
His name is Thatri, not "that bastard".

603
00:50:18,160 --> 00:50:21,720
Even though he deceived us,
his real name is still Thatri.

604
00:50:21,800 --> 00:50:23,400
Even after all this,

605
00:50:23,480 --> 00:50:26,800
you're still so loyal to him, Nid?

606
00:50:26,880 --> 00:50:28,360
Just tell me what happened.

607
00:50:29,040 --> 00:50:32,680
Mr. Thatri is doing fine,
but something happened this morning.

608
00:50:33,280 --> 00:50:35,920
Someone poisoned Mr. Thatri's cellmate.

609
00:50:37,400 --> 00:50:39,120
But he's perfectly fine.

610
00:50:39,200 --> 00:50:40,640
But it's strange.

611
00:50:41,160 --> 00:50:43,880
Whenever we brought up the incident,
he would change the subject,

612
00:50:43,960 --> 00:50:45,680
as if he didn't want us to worry.

613
00:50:45,760 --> 00:50:47,440
With his foul mouth,

614
00:50:48,080 --> 00:50:49,200
terrible attitude,

615
00:50:49,280 --> 00:50:51,640
and nosy habit,

616
00:50:52,280 --> 00:50:53,880
he must have plenty of enemies.

617
00:50:54,720 --> 00:50:57,960
I wouldn't be surprised
if someone tried to poison him.

618
00:50:59,720 --> 00:51:01,360
The only reason he's staying quiet

619
00:51:01,440 --> 00:51:04,040
is because he's probably scared
out of his wits.

620
00:51:04,120 --> 00:51:06,360
He just didn't want us to worry about him.

621
00:51:07,240 --> 00:51:10,960
Even if he isn't the real Mr. Thatri,
he has been truly good to us.

622
00:51:12,600 --> 00:51:16,080
Stop sucking up to him.
Nid, he's no longer your boss.

623
00:51:16,840 --> 00:51:18,520
Don't overdo it.

624
00:51:20,360 --> 00:51:22,000
But whatever.

625
00:51:22,560 --> 00:51:24,960
I'll cook Mee Hoon for him daily

626
00:51:25,600 --> 00:51:28,240
to ensure he doesn't get poisoned again.

627
00:51:28,320 --> 00:51:29,680
Do you really mean that?

628
00:51:29,760 --> 00:51:31,120
Of course, I do.

629
00:51:31,720 --> 00:51:33,680
I can't stand his face,

630
00:51:33,760 --> 00:51:37,360
but he did save my life once.
I haven't forgotten that.

631
00:51:38,520 --> 00:51:40,400
Besides, I'll let him experience

632
00:51:41,040 --> 00:51:44,960
the best Mee Hoon in Phuket.

633
00:51:46,560 --> 00:51:48,760
He should consider it a rare privilege.

634
00:51:57,520 --> 00:51:58,920
Uncle Ree…

635
00:52:11,560 --> 00:52:13,200
THALANG PROVINCIAL POLICE STATION

636
00:52:13,280 --> 00:52:15,080
Please sign right here.

637
00:52:21,200 --> 00:52:22,760
All done. You are free to go.

638
00:52:22,840 --> 00:52:23,880
Thank you.

639
00:52:29,040 --> 00:52:31,600
Thank you both so much for bailing me out.

640
00:52:34,640 --> 00:52:36,880
You've been in a cell for days,

641
00:52:36,960 --> 00:52:38,960
but you're still as handsome as ever.

642
00:52:39,040 --> 00:52:41,560
Not even prison bars
can ruin Uncle Ree's good looks.

643
00:52:42,920 --> 00:52:46,840
Hmm. Please ignore her.
She's just talking nonsense.

644
00:52:48,480 --> 00:52:50,880
And you don't need to thank us.

645
00:52:50,960 --> 00:52:52,600
We were only sent here to do this.

646
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:05,480
Thank you for helping me.

647
00:53:07,600 --> 00:53:10,000
I did it purely
out of humanitarian reasons,

648
00:53:11,320 --> 00:53:13,320
so don't look too much into it.

649
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:15,800
If you really want to repay me,

650
00:53:18,120 --> 00:53:20,760
just stop lying to people, sir.

651
00:53:24,600 --> 00:53:26,080
Why are you calling me "sir"?

652
00:53:28,920 --> 00:53:30,800
Then what else am I supposed to call you?

653
00:53:31,400 --> 00:53:32,720
Uncle Ree.

654
00:53:32,800 --> 00:53:36,480
Can you call me "Uncle Ree"
like you used to? I want to hear it.

655
00:53:37,160 --> 00:53:38,400
I can't.

656
00:53:39,120 --> 00:53:41,520
Because you are no longer my relative.

657
00:53:43,000 --> 00:53:44,560
I admit to everything I did wrong,

658
00:53:44,640 --> 00:53:48,040
but I never meant any harm to you
or anyone in the Som Song Saeng House.

659
00:53:48,120 --> 00:53:49,560
You still got some money out of us.

660
00:53:49,640 --> 00:53:52,280
If I truly had malicious intent,
I would've got more than that.

661
00:53:57,720 --> 00:53:59,800
I did everything

662
00:54:00,560 --> 00:54:02,880
because the real Thatri Vorapat
asked me to.

663
00:54:03,840 --> 00:54:06,120
My friend you met in Bangkok

664
00:54:06,200 --> 00:54:07,520
is your actual uncle.

665
00:54:09,760 --> 00:54:12,560
What's up, Leopard? So you found me here

666
00:54:12,640 --> 00:54:14,920
because you can't handle
my crazy family in Phuket?

667
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:16,120
Huh?

668
00:54:17,800 --> 00:54:19,360
You're from Phuket, Uncle?

669
00:54:20,120 --> 00:54:21,880
I'm from Phuket as well.

670
00:54:24,120 --> 00:54:27,560
And his mother is the woman named Suang.

671
00:54:29,720 --> 00:54:31,160
The grandchild of the wealthy Som

672
00:54:31,240 --> 00:54:33,000
actually does her own cooking?

673
00:54:33,080 --> 00:54:35,280
Do you know my grandfather, Auntie?

674
00:54:36,960 --> 00:54:39,960
Uh… Well,

675
00:54:40,040 --> 00:54:42,760
the Adisuan family is elite in Phuket.

676
00:54:42,840 --> 00:54:44,840
Everyone has heard of them.

677
00:54:47,680 --> 00:54:49,440
How can I believe you again?

678
00:54:51,160 --> 00:54:52,640
Then give me a chance.

679
00:54:54,280 --> 00:54:56,120
I will prove it to you.

680
00:55:01,360 --> 00:55:05,280
But right now,
there's something urgent I must do,

681
00:55:05,360 --> 00:55:07,480
and I need your help.

682
00:55:08,600 --> 00:55:09,960
What is it?

683
00:55:10,600 --> 00:55:12,640
I need you to get close to Mr. Vijarn,

684
00:55:12,720 --> 00:55:14,360
so you can spy on his movements.

685
00:55:23,520 --> 00:55:24,880
Miss Rajit.

686
00:55:24,960 --> 00:55:26,480
Have you heard the news?

687
00:55:27,000 --> 00:55:29,800
Your friends have already
bailed Mr. Thatri out.

688
00:55:30,400 --> 00:55:34,360
Primprao and Nareewan? I had no idea.

689
00:55:34,440 --> 00:55:36,880
I've been out working since this morning,

690
00:55:36,960 --> 00:55:38,360
running errands everywhere.

691
00:55:39,560 --> 00:55:41,400
I have such a terrible headache.

692
00:55:42,960 --> 00:55:44,920
Your friends probably fell for his tricks.

693
00:55:46,200 --> 00:55:48,400
But you should be careful, Miss Rajit.

694
00:55:48,480 --> 00:55:51,440
I'm worried that imposter
might return to deceive you again.

695
00:55:53,640 --> 00:55:55,080
There's no way.

696
00:55:55,160 --> 00:55:58,200
I have so much work on my plate right now,

697
00:55:58,280 --> 00:56:00,080
I don't have time to see anyone.

698
00:56:00,160 --> 00:56:03,360
Besides, though he isn't a good person,

699
00:56:04,120 --> 00:56:06,720
he used to help me with a lot of work.

700
00:56:07,920 --> 00:56:09,480
Now that he's gone,

701
00:56:10,440 --> 00:56:13,200
I realize just how heavy the workload is.

702
00:56:14,640 --> 00:56:16,840
Just tell me, Miss Rajit.

703
00:56:18,320 --> 00:56:20,560
Is there anything I can do to help?

704
00:56:21,360 --> 00:56:24,600
I will do whatever you ask
without a single hesitation.

705
00:56:24,680 --> 00:56:26,000
-But--
-Miss Rajit.

706
00:56:39,200 --> 00:56:40,720
You already know

707
00:56:41,880 --> 00:56:43,440
how I feel about you.

708
00:56:45,240 --> 00:56:47,560
Your problems are my problems.

709
00:56:50,840 --> 00:56:52,600
Please don't push me away.

710
00:57:10,800 --> 00:57:13,600
If things between
Mr. Vijarn and me go any further…

711
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:15,160
Are you actually accepting his love?

712
00:57:15,240 --> 00:57:17,840
Mr. Vijarn is just a second-class lawyer.

713
00:57:17,920 --> 00:57:19,520
But his legal career

714
00:57:19,600 --> 00:57:22,480
helped him build connections,
which led him into business.

715
00:57:22,560 --> 00:57:23,760
An illegal business.

716
00:57:23,840 --> 00:57:26,560
If you want to play a big game,
you must be bold.

717
00:57:26,640 --> 00:57:28,960
Everything is completely under control.

718
00:57:29,040 --> 00:57:30,080
I've always trusted you.

719
00:57:30,160 --> 00:57:31,640
No matter what,

720
00:57:31,720 --> 00:57:32,880
don't agree to get engaged.

721
00:57:32,960 --> 00:57:34,360
I worry about you so much, Rajit.

722
00:57:34,440 --> 00:57:37,600
<i>You say you're worried,</i>
<i>but you never make a move.</i>

723
00:57:37,680 --> 00:57:40,000
After all, we aren't even related anymore.

724
00:57:40,080 --> 00:57:41,720
In that case, I'm getting engaged.

725
00:57:41,800 --> 00:57:42,800
Rajit, don't do this.

726
00:57:42,880 --> 00:57:44,520
This has to be a grand event.

727
00:57:44,600 --> 00:57:47,240
Every influential figure in Phuket
will be at our celebration.

728
00:57:47,320 --> 00:57:49,480
Whatever you think is best.

729
00:58:17,120 --> 00:58:20,400
Subtitle translation by:
Khathathong Thongtumlueng
